rue]}" ssr client="load" opts="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FlowerBadge&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:true}" await-children><span style="align-items:center;align-self:center;border-radius:999px;border-style:solid;border-width:1px;box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-flex;flex-shrink:0;font-family:&#x27;SN Pro Variable&#x27;, system-ui, sans-serif;font-weight:700;justify-content:center;letter-spacing:0.1em;line-height:1;max-width:100%;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;width:fit-content;font-size:10px;padding:4px 9px;background-color:color-mix(in srgb, #E73C30 12%, transparent);border-color:transparent;color:#E73C30">Privacy</span><!--astro:end--></astro-island> <h1 class="privacy__title" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Privacy first, <br class="privacy__title-break" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>not privacy theater
</h1> <p class="privacy__lede" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Your conversation history and AI analysis stay on your machine.
          Delivery records, uploaded evidence, and the setup files you choose to
          sync have a separate home in the cloud.
</p> <p class="privacy__lede" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
You should know what Blume stores, where it lives, and what changes
          when you change a setting.
</p> </header> <article class="privacy__body" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <section aria-labelledby="local" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <h2 id="local" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Your conversation history stays local</h2> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Blume reads supported coding agents’ session files and imports their
            conversations into a local database. That database is not uploaded
            as a cloud archive of your chats.
</p> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Imported messages, signals, evidence excerpts, suggestions, and
            processing history remain on your device. Your setup inventory,
            local file mappings, and generated Wrapped cards and summaries also
            stay local.
</p> </section> <section aria-labelledby="processing" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <h2 id="processing" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>AI analysis stays on your machine</h2> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Blume does not send conversation or project context to the cloud for
            AI analysis. Your imported conversations and local analysis records
            remain on your device.
</p> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Files you choose to sync and content you submit to Deliveries are
            separate cloud records. Local analysis does not mean that every
            Blume feature stores its data only on your machine.
</p> </section> <section aria-labelledby="deliveries" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <h2 id="deliveries" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Deliveries keeps a shared cloud record</h2> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Project settings, plans, tasks, progress updates, reviews, and test
            results sent to Deliveries live in Blume’s hosted workspace ledger.
            Text, code, or paths included in an update become part of that cloud
            record.
</p> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Uploaded screenshots and test artifacts are stored in the cloud.
            Tests can run on your machine and still upload their results and
            evidence. Hosted tests run in a cloud sandbox against a reachable
            target.
</p> <div class="privacy__card" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Your imported conversation database stays local. Content submitted
              as a delivery update or evidence is stored separately in the
              cloud.
</p> </div> </section> <section aria-labelledby="setup-sync" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <h2 id="setup-sync" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Setup sync includes file contents</h2> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Setup artifact sync stores snapshots of the files you choose to
            sync, along with their relative paths, in your cloud account. Sync
            sends file content, not just filenames or counts.
</p> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Each device keeps its own absolute path mapping locally. Removing a
            sync mapping on one device does not delete the cloud item; deleting
            that item is a separate action.
</p> </section> <section aria-labelledby="accounts" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <h2 id="accounts" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Accounts and connected services</h2> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
The desktop stores its account session and GitHub token locally
            using operating-system encryption. Sign-in also uses remote account
            and authorization records, and connected services keep their own
            remote authorization records.
</p> </section> <section aria-labelledby="telemetry" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <h2 id="telemetry" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Aggregate usage and product diagnostics</h2> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Blume sends aggregate usage counts and product diagnostics, such as
            usage events, app version, platform, timings, and sanitized error
            details, to help operate and improve the service.
</p> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Diagnostics are designed to exclude conversation content and
            credentials. These diagnostics are separate from the delivery
            updates, evidence, and synced files described above.
</p> </section> <section aria-labelledby="control" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <h2 id="control" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Know what your choices change</h2> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>You can:</p> <ul class="privacy__list privacy__list--check" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <li data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Choose which setup files to sync</li><li data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Remove a setup sync mapping on a device</li><li data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Delete local Blume data</li><li data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Remove connected accounts</li><li data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>Remove Blume from your system</li> </ul> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Deleting local Blume data does not delete cloud delivery records or
            uploaded evidence. Removing setup sync removes the mapping on that
            device; deleting the cloud item is a separate action. Feature
            availability can vary by app version.
</p> <p data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
For a feature-by-feature guide, read <a href="/docs/local-and-cloud-data" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>What stays local and what goes to the cloud</a>.
</p> </section> </article> <footer class="privacy__closing" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3> <p class="privacy__closing-statement" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>
Privacy should not require trust alone. It should be understandable
          from how the product is built.
</p> <p class="privacy__closing-note" data-astro-cid-fb3qbcs3>That's the standard we aim to meet.</p> </footer> </div> </main> <footer class="site-footer" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> <picture class="site-footer__media" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> <source media="(min-width: 1440px)" srcset="/images/sidecar/bg-3072.avif" type="image/avif" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> <source media="(min-width: 768px)" srcset="/images/sidecar/bg-1280.avif" type="image/avif" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> <source media="(min-width: 1440px)" srcset="/images/sidecar/bg-3072.webp" type="image/webp" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> <source media="(min-width: 768px)" srcset="/images/sidecar/bg-1280.webp" type="image/webp" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> <img src="/images/sidecar/bg-768.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> </picture> <div class="site-footer__shade" aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v></div> <div class="site-footer__inner" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> <div class="site-footer__logo" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> <link rel="preload" as="image" href="/images/flowers/red-tulip/icon.png"/><span class="blume-lockup blume-lockup--footer blume-lockup--on-photo" style="--blume-mark-start-trim:calc(var(--blume-frame, 34px) * 0.35897436);--blume-mark-end-trim:calc(var(--blume-frame, 34px) * 0.30128205)" role="img" aria-label="Blume"><img class="blume-lockup__mark" src="/images/flowers/red-tulip/icon.png" alt="" draggable="false"/><span class="blume-lockup__word" aria-hidden="true">blume</span></span> </div> <p class="site-footer__statement" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v>Know what your agents built.</p> <div class="site-footer__bottom" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> <nav class="site-footer__links" aria-label="Footer" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v> <a href="/" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v>Home</a><a href="/docs" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v>Docs</a><a href="/blog" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v>Blog</a><a href="/about" data-astro-cid-gcn2mc3v>About</a><a href="/careers" data-astro-cid-g